        "original_id": "5ef9419f-cf2c-54e5-8588-8bf547bbcb41",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: New Faces of 1952\n- People: Paul Lynde, Alice Ghostley, Eartha Kitt, Robert Clary, Carol Lawrence, Ronny Graham, Mel Brooks, Sheldon Harnick\n- Roles: performer, writer, lyricist, actress\n- Topics: career beginnings, musical theatre, television\n\nFacts:\n- New Faces of 1952 helped jump-start the careers of young performers including Paul Lynde, Alice Ghostley, Eartha Kitt, Robert Clary, Carol Lawrence, and Ronny Graham.\n- New Faces of 1952 also helped jump-start the careers of performer and writer Mel Brooks, who was billed as Melvin Brooks, and lyricist Sheldon Harnick.\n- Carol Lawrence was born on September 5, 1932.\n- Carol Lawrence is an American actress most often associated with musical theatre.\n- Carol Lawrence has also appeared extensively on television.",
